+# [P0] Restore Render primary-node deploy — poetry.lock missing at Docker COPY
+
+## Task ID
+`bridge-20261027-render-poetry-lock`
+
+## Target repository
+`Supremeai-bd/supremeai-core` (tracked on the public `supremeai-open` task board per federation policy).
+
+## Severity
+**P0 — production deployment is broken.** The primary Render service cannot build; every auto-deploy attempt fails.
+
+## Verified evidence (pulled live via MCP tower, 2026-10-26 ~16:45 UTC)
+- `render_service_health(srv-dau7c9ek1f9s73almn0g)` → `lastDeployStatus: "build_failed"` (service `supremeai-primary-node`, repo `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-core`, env `docker`, dockerfilePath `Dockerfile`, healthCheckPath `/health/live`, region singapore, plan free).
+- `render_get_logs(type=build, level=error, text="poetry.lock", window 2026-10-25T04:00Z–10:30Z)` → **8 error entries**, including:
+  - `2026-10-25T04:32:39.166Z #9 ERROR: failed to calculate checksum of ref ...: "/poetry.lock": not found`
+  - `2026-10-25T04:47:22.389Z #9 ERROR: failed to calculate checksum ... "/poetry.lock": not found`
+  - `2026-10-25T05:00:58.034Z #10 ERROR: failed to calculate checksum ... "/poetry.lock": not found`
+- Root error line (per audit report): `Dockerfile:13 COPY pyproject.toml poetry.lock ./` — the build context contains `pyproject.toml` but **no `poetry.lock`**.
+
+## Why this blocks production
+- Every commit to `supremeai-core` main auto-triggers a Render deploy that fails → the running container (if any) is a stale image; no code fix since Oct 25 has reached the primary node.
+- The dependency contract is split: `requirements.txt` (ad-hoc, limited) vs `pyproject.toml`/`poetry.lock` (Docker). There is no single reproducible dependency source.
+
+## Remediation plan (smallest safe change first)
+1. **Restore or generate `poetry.lock`** in the repo root of `supremeai-core` and commit it (or deliberately drop poetry and pin everything in `requirements.txt` — pick ONE source of truth; do not keep both half-configured).
+2. Make `Dockerfile` COPY match reality (either `COPY pyproject.toml poetry.lock ./` with the lock present, or install from the pinned requirements file).
+3. Build the exact Docker image in CI on every push to main (build must be a required check, not skipped/masked).
+4. Redeploy `supremeai-primary-node` and confirm `lastDeployStatus: "live"` + `/health/live` 200 with the NEW image.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- [ ] `poetry.lock` (or the chosen pinned dependency manifest) committed at repo root
+- [ ] Render deploy of `srv-dau7c9ek1f9s73almn0g` reaches `live`
+- [ ] CI builds the same Docker image deterministically (no `|| true` on install steps)
+- [ ] Dependency source is singular and documented in the repo README
+
